# K8 - Stressor x component audit. Kata sandbox sketch (plan section 3.6).
# [K8-nn] sketch IDs are recognised by validate_architecture / trace and ignored by the
# CI adl-coverage gate. Never [TR-*]; promotion is decided only at K12 (architecture/REVIEW.md).
DESCRIPTION K8 - the stressor matrix points at real files, and every source of variability in the code is a stressor
CATEGORY Architectural Capabilities
NAMESPACE TrK8NS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall K8 Sandbox AS trk8
    DEFINE COMPONENT Incidence Matrix AS matrix
    DEFINE COMPONENT Stressor List AS stressors

# Course pp. 66-67: a stressor x component matrix that names its residues. architecture-style.adl
# already has it (S1..S7) and TR-E1 checks the residue IDs. Nothing checks the other half: the files
# the incidence lines point at. A renamed file leaves a matrix that reads well and points nowhere.
ASSERT(Incidence Matrix: every source file named in the stressor incidence lines of architecture-style.adl exists) # [K8-01]

# The list is only as complete as the sources of variability someone thought of. The audit reads them
# from the code (an engines range, a value read once at load, a nested CLI call) and requires a
# stressor line that names each. It finds three the seven stressors leave out.
ASSERT(Stressor List: every source of variability found in the code is named by a stressor line with a residue) # [K8-02]

# Not re-asserted, answered with existing evidence (answers.md): the residue rule (TR-E1), harness
# API change (S1: TR-C5, TR-C1), missing native binding (S2: TR-R1, TR-R3), 20k scale (S4: TR-P1,
# TR-P2 and the weekly benchmark job).
